\" href=\"#p-498473-additional-information-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccount: \u003ca href=\"mailto:dakshivikas@gmail.com\"\u003edakshivikas@gmail.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498473-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-11\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498473-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-11\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T04:33:41.371Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":9,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":45.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172696,"topic_slug":"can-t-reach-your-computer-on-macos","display_username":"Vikas Dakshi","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139277,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/can-t-reach-your-computer-on-macos/172696/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true,"can_vote":false},{"id":498735,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-23T04:33:16.746Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and the screenshots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGood news first. The Grok Bot computer on our side is working fine. Each Recover and Reset did create a new computer, and it came up in about a minute. The problem is that your Mac’s network can’t resolve the address the app uses to connect to it. This lookup happens on your side, so Recover and Reset won’t fix it. For now, it’s best not to press Reset again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry switching your Mac to public DNS:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSystem Settings → Network.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect your active connection (Wi-Fi or Ethernet) → Details.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDNS tab.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUnder DNS Servers, click + and add \u003ccode\u003e1.1.1.1\u003c/code\u003e, then click + again and add \u003ccode\u003e8.8.8.8\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOK.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot (menu bar icon → Quit, or \u003ccode\u003eCmd+Q\u003c/code\u003e). Just closing the window isn’t enough.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot again and wait about 2 minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want to test the lookup directly, open Terminal and run:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003enslookup test.us12.cursorvm.com\nnslookup test.us12.cursorvm.com 1.1.1.1\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the first command fails but the second returns an address, that confirms it’s a DNS issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you can’t change DNS, switching to a different ISP can help. A hotspot from the same provider usually won’t help. After switching networks, fully quit and reopen the app again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if the Can’t reach your computer banner disappears after step 7. If not, please send the output of both commands.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T04:33:16.746Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172696,"topic_slug":"can-t-reach-your-computer-on-macos","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/can-t-reach-your-computer-on-macos/172696/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":true,"topic_accepted_answer":true}],"stream":[498473,498735]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"“Can’t reach your computer” on macOS","id":172696,"title":"“Can’t reach your computer” on macOS","posts_count":2,"created_at":"2026-09-22T19:01:32.990Z","views":22,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-23T04:33:16.746Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"can-t-reach-your-computer-on-macos","category_id":6,"word_count":485,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":139277,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/2/b/2bc066a75dc10aa724c2f59d889d114ce3fb4d32_2_1023x289.png","slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_172696","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_